&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Influence Executive&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;Department:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt; Influence&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;Location: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;London&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;Contact type: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;12-Month Fixed Term Contract&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;Full Time/Part time:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt; Full Time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;Reporting into: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;Business Director&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Onefluence is seeking a dynamic and trend-savvy Senior Influencer Executive to join our team dedicated to L&#39;Oréal. The ideal candidate will be responsible for driving successful influencer marketing campaigns that align with L&#39;Oréal&#39;s brand objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior Influencer Executive, you will lead influencer strategy and campaign execution across social platforms to amplify brand awareness, drive engagement, and grow our community within the beauty space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be responsible for managing influencer relationships, developing creative campaign concepts, and ensuring brand alignment with both macro and micro creators.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influencer Strategy &amp;amp; Campaign Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute influencer campaigns for new product launches, brand awareness, and seasonal initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and onboard relevant beauty influencers (macro, micro, and nano) across TikTok, Instagram, YouTube, and emerging platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and manage influencer briefs, contracts, timelines, and budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee influencer content production to ensure brand tone, aesthetic, and compliance with marketing guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with top-tier beauty influencers, talent managers, and agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the main point of contact for influencer collaborations and ongoing partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyse influencer campaign performance using analytics tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver insights and recommendations to optimize future campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on ROI, engagement metrics, and audience growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with PR, social media, e-commerce, and creative teams to ensure consistent messaging and amplification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support integrated marketing initiatives that combine influencer, content, and brand storytelling.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-3 years of experience in influencer marketing, preferably within the beauty, cosmetics, or lifestyle industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of social media platforms and influencer ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, negotiation, and relationship management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset with experience using tools like Traackr, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative eye for beauty trends, social storytelling, and content aesthetics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple projects and stakeholders in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing network of beauty influencers or creators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with paid and seeding influencer amplification or affiliate programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of emerging platforms (e.g., TikTok Shop, Threads, YouTube Shorts).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days annual leave + 1 Volunteer Day &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bupa Healthcare&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced Maternity, Adoption and Shared Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have a Flexible Working Model with core working hours: 10am – 4pm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 1.5:1 Matching Pension Structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellbeing and Health: Up to £25.00 per month towards physical or online exercise class membership, Unmind membership, LifeWorks tool and annual eye tests and development budgets and Wellbeing incentives and activities throughout the year &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Season Ticket Loan and Cycle to Work Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Our ambition is to attract the very best diverse talent to Ogilvy, and to be the employer of choice in the UK. We want everyone to feel welcome when they join us, and once they’re here, for them to want to stay with us, grow their career, and to feel they belong with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNoSpacing&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and we’re committed to creating an inclusive, welcoming environment for everyone who wants to work at Ogilvy. For us, diversity, equity and inclusion is integrated into everything that we do. We believe that for creativity to flourish, everything about how we work must have diversity at its core. Your race, colour, ethnic, religion, gender, gender identity, national origin, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability, have no bearing on our hiring decisions, but we encourage everyone to feel free to express their true selves in an environment we are consistently striving to make as inclusive as possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNoSpacing&quot;&gt;We aim to facilitate an accessible and positive application experience for all candidates. If you require any adjustments from us to support you through the process or expect to require any adjustments to working conditions to be able to best perform in the role, please let us know. We are happy to consider all reasonable adjustments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNoSpacing&quot;&gt;If you live with a disability and you would like to take advantage of our offer of a guaranteed interview under the Disability Confident Scheme, please ensure you fill out our voluntary Equal Opportunities Questionnaire when applying.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; UK (remote)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reachdesk is the first truly end-to-end global SaaS gifting and swag platform, helping B2B companies create meaningful connections with prospects, customers, and employees, while driving measurable ROI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe gifting is more than just a transaction: it’s about building genuine human connections that fuel business growth. Whether it’s engaging prospects, celebrating customers, or recognizing employees, our platform makes it easy to deliver personalized gifts, branded swag, and unforgettable event &amp;amp; brand experiences at scale through automated sourcing, storage, and global delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trusted by many of the most recognized names in technology and SaaS, Reachdesk integrates effortlessly with marketing, sales, and HRIS tech stacks and is powered by our world-class team across New York, London, and Lisbon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re growing, and we’re currently looking for a Senior Product Manager to join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Manager at Reachdesk, you’ll play a pivotal role in shaping the Reachdesk Platform. You will be accountable for turning complex customer and business problems into software products that deliver measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Chief Product Officer, you’ll lead product initiatives end-to-end,&amp;nbsp; from identifying and deeply understanding the right problems to solve, through discovery and delivery, to launch, adoption, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll operate with a high degree of autonomy, proactively building context across customers, the market, internal stakeholders, data, and technology to understand what Reachdesk needs to achieve its goals. You’ll also make sound decisions when the path forward isn’t obvious.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll partner closely with Engineering and Design and work across the wider business to create alignment, communicate decisions clearly, and ensure what we build is successfully launched, adopted, and delivers the outcomes we set out to achieve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy solving difficult problems, taking ownership, and moving comfortably between customer, technical, and business conversations, you’ll thrive in this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set product direction and priorities&lt;/strong&gt;, bringing together company goals, internal stakeholder needs, customer insight, market context, data, and technical considerations to focus on the highest-impact opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define problems and experiences before solutions&lt;/strong&gt;, creating clear stories, journeys, and shared context so the Design and Engineering teams understand the problem and intended outcomes before determining the solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead product initiatives end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt;, from discovery and solution definition through delivery, rollout, and iteration, partnering with Engineering to manage scope, make pragmatic trade-offs, and deliver valuable solutions at pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make sound product decisions and trade-offs&lt;/strong&gt;, balancing customer and business needs, commercial impact, user experience, and technical considerations while aligning the wider business on compromises, priorities, and expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop product opportunities with external partners&lt;/strong&gt;, building relationships with technology partners to uncover mutual opportunities, shape integrations, align roadmaps, and navigate the product and commercial considerations required to bring them to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Orchestrate successful launches and adoption&lt;/strong&gt;, working across Sales, Marketing, Customer Success, Services, Logistics, Finance, Legal, and other teams to ensure the business is ready and customers realise value from what we build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communicate with clarity throughout&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring leadership and teams across Reachdesk understand product decisions, progress, risks, changes, and results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong track record of &lt;strong&gt;owning B2B SaaS products end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt;, from identifying the right problems through delivery, adoption, and measurable customer and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a &lt;strong&gt;strong problem solver&lt;/strong&gt; who gets to the root of complex problems, brings structure to ambiguity, and uses evidence and judgement to determine the right path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You operate with &lt;strong&gt;independence and initiative&lt;/strong&gt;: you seek out the customers, stakeholders, data, and context you need rather than waiting for direction, while staying anchored to Reachdesk’s goals and priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have &lt;strong&gt;strong business and commercial awareness&lt;/strong&gt; and are curious about how the wider company operates, allowing you to understand competing needs and make pragmatic decisions beyond the boundaries of Product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re &lt;strong&gt;technically fluent enough to work effectively with Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;, understand systems, integrations, and constraints, ask the right questions, and contribute meaningfully to solution and scope decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an &lt;strong&gt;exceptional communicator&lt;/strong&gt;, able to create clarity, influence decisions, surface difficult trade-offs, and adapt how you communicate across customers, engineers, leadership, and teams throughout the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable &lt;strong&gt;operating externally as well as internally&lt;/strong&gt;, building productive relationships with technology partners, uncovering shared opportunities, influencing without authority, and navigating product, technical, and commercial conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong sense of &lt;strong&gt;product and user experience&lt;/strong&gt;, caring about the coherence and quality of the complete experience rather than whether individual requirements or features have simply been delivered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary with generous stock options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension with employer contributions (NEST)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Affordable Private Medical Insurance, including mental health support and fast access to care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO that increases the longer you’re with us, plus extra flexibility for life’s unexpected moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuinely collaborative culture with innovative, fun, and ambitious people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reachdesk believes that a diverse team helps us achieve our mission faster, and so we welcome applicants from all backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Privacy Policy: We process personal information submitted as part of your application in accordance with the Reachdesk Candidate Privacy Notice. Please review Reachdesk’s Privacy Policy here: &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.reachdesk.com/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;www.reachdesk.com/candidate-privacy-policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position: Account Specialist&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Account Specialist &lt;/strong&gt;position is a remote, work-from-home role, as are all positions at Acceleration Partners (a structure central to our culture and vision to change the work/life paradigm). Some travel may be required for client meetings, internal meetings, conferences, and other events. &lt;strong&gt;Please note: &lt;/strong&gt;This position requires verbal and written fluency in German.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;Account Specialist&lt;/strong&gt;, you will provide white glove service to diverse brands investing in influencer marketing campaigns. This role is particularly focused on campaign execution, including but not limited to driving influencer recruitment, managing influencer partnerships, and owning campaign deliverables, tracking, and reporting. The Account Specialist will also drive strategy by analyzing campaign performance, identifying success areas and/or challenge areas, and proactively implementing strategic measures to continuously optimize programs towards goals and objectives.&lt;br&gt;The successful candidate will have strong experience in developing and managing successful, KPI-driven influencer marketing campaigns for consumer products and/or services companies. They will have working knowledge of the overall partner marketing landscape, including affiliate, and the ability to both develop comprehensive strategy as well as capably execute. The successful candidate will be a self-starter that can confidently plug in to any challenging situation with ease and can balance competing priorities well. The Account Specialist must be flexible, willing and able to pivot quickly, and excited to operate successfully in an “intrapreneurial” situation. This person will also have a history of working well with their peers, quickly establishing relationships easily and leading through influence.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll work closely with your manager and peers to maximize program effectiveness and create opportunities for growth.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Top 5 Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;INFLUENCER RECRUITMENT, NEGOTIATING &amp;amp; ONBOARDING –&lt;/strong&gt;Sources new partnership opportunities and creates influencer casting lists. Diligently vets opportunities to ensure brand alignment, authenticity and relevancy prior to presenting to client for approval. Conducts outreach to approved partners and skillfully garners their engagement and participation in the campaign, negotiating when necessary. Supports influencers through campaign onboarding by developing and providing resources to streamline processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;INFLUENCER PARTNERSHIPS MANAGEMENT &lt;/strong&gt;– Crafts program-wide influencer communications and vital creator resources. Guides influencers on content strategy and creation. Works with influencers to develop content timelines and ensures influencers stay on track with the schedules discussed. Collects content drafts and leads the content review process, including screening to ensure FTC guidelines are met. Closely works with influencers to adjust content strategy as needed, troubleshooting any signs of poor performance to optimize campaign towards goals and objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AUDITING, REPORTING &amp;amp; ANALYSIS &lt;/strong&gt;– Accountable for auditing program content to ensure compliance with FTC regulations and brand guidelines. Ensures content is tracked accurately and regularly shared with client, along with placement insights, partner insights, and campaign pace towards KPI goals. Performs robust analysis of influencer campaigns using both social analytics and conversion metrics to identify performance trends and areas of opportunity. Proactively provides actionable recommendations to client backed by data and continuously refines strategy to drive growth at scale. Supports team in creation of customized strategy plans, detailed campaign performance summaries and comprehensive hindsight presentations that are delivered to clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLIENT SERVICE &amp;amp; COMMUNICATION&lt;/strong&gt;- Consistently provides superior client service and escalates issues or key risks as appropriate. Works to ensure client develops trust in our team by delivering client outputs and communications in the AP way, consistently maintaining quality, accuracy, and precision. Develops and nurtures excellent relationships, supports team in promoting very high client satisfaction and retention rates, and an average 8.5 client rating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PORTFOLIO MANAGEMENT&lt;/strong&gt;- Own and manage client tasks with minimal supervision, ensuring deadlines are met and tasks are completed accurately. Manages multiple campaigns with solid organizational skills and the ability to focus on and prioritize tasks based on client objectives, flagging any potential delays and keeping the team informed. Has full grasp of each client’s scope of work, delivering what is due under terms; maintains ability to identify new opportunities to drive client success while conjunctively identifying possible goal misalignments, getting to the root of an issue, and working with their team to bring solutions to resolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BY 3 MONTHS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Account Specialist is contributing across a portfolio of influencer programs, collaborating with their team closely to ensure strong alignment with the campaign strategy in place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are working with key client contacts to ensure brand alignment with recruitment efforts and content creation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have become familiar with AP’s tools and solutions and are equipped to conduct casting for prospective influencers, execute content timelines with influencers, audit content, and ensure performance is tracked and measured.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By 6 MONTHS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are owning execution of the day-to-day operations of multiple influencer programs with little guidance from your team, including reporting, processing applications, recruiting and casting creators, and crafting partner communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging client or team situations are being managed with guidance from managers and directors collaborating closely to bring a solutions-oriented approach to these situations proactively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are regularly analyzing client data and strategically leveraging insights to optimize campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client accounts are being handled effectively and strategically, without dropping any balls, and clients are aware of and pleased with this outcome. Clients are being serviced profitably with AP targets, client KPI’s being met, and an average 8.5 client rating is being upheld across campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will regularly present new campaign ideas to managers and demonstrate a clear understanding of program performance&lt;/li&gt;
